-- Serre criterion, direct implication: final assembly (agent G).
-- SerreLocalIso: isomorphisms are local on the target (lem:localiso); the
-- restricted maps are read through SliceMap's lattice and section traces
-- (Piece.lat-at, Piece.sharp-at by refl), the rest uses order lemmas,
-- sheaf gluing/separation and Iso's equivalence lemmas by name.
-- SerreCanonicalMap: an affine-target recognition lemma (Recognise) and the
-- canonical map over D_A(f); openings are the structural carriers of slices,
-- Spec A, Affine's fractions and SpecMap's lattice map (gamma(D_A f) = D(f)),
-- and the one-step definitions of composites, Gamma and cut.
-- SerreAffineness: the two covers of a partition of unity, the principal
-- theorem, affineness as a proposition, and Serre: the theorem, using
-- SerrePartitionCover and SerreRingLocalisation directly; it opens only the
-- PrincipalCover/AffineCover signatures, the qcqs property and the carrier
-- aliases (open-f, Loc) of the ring lemma's statement.
-- No quotient, localisation-universality, gluing or extensionality proof is
-- reopened by these declarations.
